Subject: [PATCH] ui/sdl2: redraw the active scanout on deferred refresh

Local follow-up to upstream 5bb16eb70701b01ae9ffe2d7e5165f5a70c5df69.
Applies to the external QEMU display dependency, not the Linux core.
The original SDL source license remains MIT.

A placeholder update queued by scanout disable can still be pending when
virtio-gpu installs and flushes its first GL scanout. The refresh timer then
draws the old pixman surface over the GL frame. Preserving scanout_mode is
not sufficient: refresh must select the active presentation source, just as
an SDL expose/resize event already does. Reuse sdl2_gl_redraw for that choice.
No guest resource contents, GPU commands, fences or events are synthesized.

--- a/ui/sdl2-gl.c
+++ b/ui/sdl2-gl.c
@@ -116,7 +116,7 @@ void sdl2_gl_refresh(DisplayChangeListener *dcl)
     graphic_hw_update(dcl->con);
     if (scon->updates && scon->real_window) {
         scon->updates = 0;
-        sdl2_gl_render_surface(scon);
+        sdl2_gl_redraw(scon);
     }
     sdl2_poll_events(scon);
 }
